                            <comment id="382738" author="adilger" created="Wed, 16 Aug 2023 23:18:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;+1 on master &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/cc48437c-ffa7-4bf7-bfa9-91401dd2d870&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/cc48437c-ffa7-4bf7-bfa9-91401dd2d870&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It may be that this is a rare race condition if the OST does not have any precreated objects right after mount and the MDS is skipping it for allocation.  I don&apos;t think it indicates any kind of serious problem.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="491264" author="sbansal" created="Fri, 13 Mar 2026 12:24:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This started failing again, any idea?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="491310" author="adilger" created="Fri, 13 Mar 2026 16:49:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;There may occasionally be failures like this, but if it started failing consistently then it may be more of a concern.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You could search for when the tests started failing:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?horizon=2332800&amp;amp;status%5B%5D=FAIL&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=7f66aa20-3db2-11e0-80c0-52540025f9af&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=a39bae60-29d2-11e6-a0ce-5254006e85c2&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?horizon=2332800&amp;amp;status%5B%5D=FAIL&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=7f66aa20-3db2-11e0-80c0-52540025f9af&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=a39bae60-29d2-11e6-a0ce-5254006e85c2&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;and then check for commits within a few days of that date to see if some patch was landed that broke the test. Then push a test patch to Gerrit to try and reproduce the failure and bisect the patches in the date range until the cause has been isolated (if it is not obvious just from looking at the list of patches) &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
